<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Diagram illustrating the effects of creatine supplementation and exercise on muscle and brain. The muscle segment highlights increased phosphocreatine, ATP regeneration, protein synthesis, and reduced oxidative stress. Exercise enhances myokine release, mitochondrial function, and muscle strength. The brain section details improved energy metabolism, antioxidant effects, neurotransmission, neurogenesis, hippocampal volume, cognitive reserve, and reduced neuroinflammation. Together, these lead to better training adaptations and cognitive improvements through the muscle-brain axis.) /K 705 0 R /P 230 0 R /Pg 221 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
